PROTECTED INVENTIONS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  1. The F5(p) prime deformation family of Lie algebras over ℤ[1/12],
     parameterized by primes p ≡ 1 (mod 12), λ_p = (p mod 12)/12.

  2. g₅(13) as a rank-5 non-crystallographic extension of F4 with
     Cartan entry -1/12, dimension 1245, and 1240 roots.

  3. Computational reflection proof architecture: Rust exact rational
     verification → Lean 4 `by decide` certificate generation.

  4. Applications of the F5(p) family in post-quantum cryptography
     using prime-indexed multiplicity vectors.

